#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Post the shell commands AI coding agents run to Discord.

Managed by Ansible (roles/cmd_center/tasks/cmd_audit.yml). Local edits are
overwritten.

Usage:
    agent-cmd-audit record                 Claude Code PostToolUse hook
    agent-cmd-audit flush [--dry-run]      post spooled records (timer)
    agent-cmd-audit canary                 spool a synthetic record (timer)

record       Reads the hook JSON on stdin, appends one line to the spool and
             returns at once. It always exits 0 and never writes to stdout, so
             it can never break or slow an agent. Registered for BOTH
             PostToolUse and PostToolUseFailure with matcher Bash: a failing
             Bash call throws, so only the failure event sees it.
flush        Seals the spool, posts one batch per run and deletes the batch
             only after Discord accepts it. Never exits non-zero for a failed
             post: a Discord outage must not turn into a unit-failure alert.
canary       Proves the whole path end to end, including Discord acceptance.
             Liveness checks on the units prove only that they ran.
--dry-run    Print the payload as JSON. Posts nothing, fetches no secret and
             deletes no batch.

What this CANNOT see, by construction:
  - commands denied or blocked before they ran (no post-hook fires at all)
  - the outcome of run_in_background commands (the hook fires when the tool
    returns, not when the command ends)
  - shell run by MCP servers, skills or plugins outside the Bash tool
  - the operator's own ! commands in the REPL

SECURITY: this is telemetry, not a tamper-proof audit log. The spool and the
agent's own settings are writable by the user the agent runs as, so an agent
with Bash can disable its own auditing. Root owning this script and its config
raises the bar; it does not close it.

Command text is untrusted and routinely holds credentials. Everything that
reaches Discord goes through sanitize_command(), which fails CLOSED: if a
secret pattern still matches after redaction, the command is withheld instead
of posted. Every payload carries allowed_mentions {"parse": []}, and the
webhook URL is never logged or put in an exception.

Configuration (environment, all optional):
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_ENABLED         0 disables recording (default 1)
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_OP_REFERENCE    1Password reference of the webhook URL
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_OP_LIB_DIR      directory holding op-killswitch.sh and
                                    op-secret-cache.sh
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_OP_TOKEN_FILE   1Password service account token file
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_STATE_DIR       spool, lock and state directory
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_PROM_FILE       node_exporter textfile collector output
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_HOST            host name shown in the footer
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_HERDR_BIN       herdr CLI path ("" disables labels)
    AGENT_CMD_AUDIT_CONFIG          KEY=VALUE file holding any of the above
                                    (/etc/default/agent-cmd-audit); the
                                    environment wins over the file
"""

